{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/evidence-review/references/experiments.md'","aggregated_output":"EXECUTION Observe actual implementation effects under explicit inputs, caller policy and authorized isolation. Contract applicability may remain unresolved during exploration; execution permission may not. A changed value or tests_passed is not a violation oracle. Exploration remains construction knowledge: a later requirement needs a separately fixed check, fresh execution and correspondence review, not retroactive relabelling. Missing capability, compilation failure, timeout, panic and a completed property comparison remain distinct. Retain failures; never precompute expected observations or alter protocol behavior to create a finding.\n\nCOMPLETION Initialization, driver compliance and observation validity belong in prerequisites, controls or diagnostics, not duplicate properties. A diagnostic control need not satisfy the principal scenario's premises or acquire a separate obligation: select formal applicability using independently declared input/policy fields before execution, retaining control output for explanation. If formally comparing distinct scenarios, express each one's actual admission and premises; incompatible histories may need separate checks. Never select scenarios by the observed result, whether reproduction succeeded, or a missing premise after execution. Role or phase readiness does not imply that earlier work has drained. Across preparation, policy changes and delivery, preserve the selected caller/transport contract; prefer one delivery path with policy-selected deferral and record only the identity, provenance and order needed for attribution. Distinguish network receipt, per-message-type queueing and handler dispatch; identify which layer the driver replaces and preserve its ordering constraints, without assuming global FIFO or arbitrary reordering. Legal in-flight work need not be emptied and does not itself invalidate an otherwise supported check. End controlled work independently of the forbidden behavior. Observe admission, completion and final state for the same operation before treating absence as bounded holds. Missing completion, identity, result events and tool timeout remain unknown. A finite tick/wait window records non-completion, not a deadline violation or infinite stalling. For a repeatable suffix, account for behavior-determining state, external schedule, queues, timers and callbacks; equal selected business fields do not close the execution. A later operation restoring progress helps locate a trigger, but may itself be required caller work.\n\nCORRELATION Monitor.admission_alias explicitly selects the declared harness prerequisite admitting operations whose completion is owed. It is not the first prerequisite by array order. Harness.prerequisites contains prerequisite events only; monitors select independent result events. ObservableProperty.identity_fields declares the stable operation identity once, using fields present at the relevant observation points. Do not repeat a result as a prerequisite or duplicate each identity equality as a Comparison. Reference conditions declare necessary predecessor relationships; unrelated prerequisites have no implicit list order. Assertions may refer to any declared prerequisite alias that actually precedes the result. Missing identity/reference fields or nonunique associations remain unknown. Independent applicability is checked before requiring unrelated history. Alias-dependent applicability follows correlation. Each operation is matched separately. A complete violating witness survives missing results in demonstrably independent operations, while coverage remains partial. Same-witness ambiguity and potentially global parse loss still block attribution. Use independent identity, not the compared value, to associate an input and output. A context expected to change cannot also be an equality filter. More complex histories need actual correlated prerequisites and results; unsupported general temporal expressions remain a stated limitation.\n\nMEANING Record comparisons in properties/outcome and scope/applicability limits separately. Identify whether decisive observations read a live object, copy, cache or caller-maintained state; an export discrepancy need not mean the active protocol state changed. Verify the observation path as required by the claim, without mandatory dual observation or private-state access. Keep unresolved contracts, counterevidence, input legality and observation differences explicit; CheckRun owns execution status. An implementation/requirement discrepancy is the investigation subject, not a conflict between requirement sources. Real contradictions remain conflicts.\n\nCONFIRMATION Reconstruct decisive prerequisite relationships from the current fixed test, actual constructors/producers and raw events. The plan's legality account is a claim to verify. Check manually prepared state, substituted call edges and identity/context/generation compatibility across stages; a constructible input or two isolated fragments do not establish one legal history. Preserve constructor queues, callbacks, lock ownership, lifecycle and caller/transport duties needed by this proposition. Use existing rationale, source_ids, counterevidence, challenged_components and exact ReviewIssues for discrepancies. Concrete incompatible inputs are attribution gaps, not merely unstudied wider scope. Local functions, injectable storage, bounded initialization and substitute schedules are legitimate when the sourced proposition permits them. Review independent oracle, event parsing, reached premises and completion together. Preserve measurements while correspondence is pending; established local results survive independent wider-history or endpoint limits without gaining broader consequences. New source counterevidence may challenge prior confirmation through existing issues and F2/F3; an unobserved system endpoint remains a limit.\nNECESSITY For a sourced safety condition S implies E, compare observed S only when independently established E is false, or use an equivalent supported implication encoding. Do not silently strengthen it to S equals E, suppress the result field through applicability, or infer eventual success from a permitted pending control.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
