{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_75","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"submission\": \"submission.json\",\n  \"summary\": \"Submitted a combined research + Candidate product for the hashicorp/raft snapshot.\\n\\nFiles (draft-relative): submission.json (the submitted product) and map.json (the referenced ConsensusAuditSpec map).\\n\\nWhat it contains:\\n- A usable core_overview with both core lines and their connection: formation = leader dispatch -> per-peer AppendEntries -> quorum match tracking under the term-start-index rule -> commit/apply (b-dispatch-logs, b-leader-replicate, b-commit-quorum, b-leader-commit-apply; f-commit-quorum, f-log-prefix); context/authority = heartbeat timeout -> candidate/pre-vote -> vote decision on term/membership/log-up-to-dateness -> step-down or deliberate transfer (b-heartbeat-timeout, b-candidate-election, b-vote-grant, b-prevote, b-leader-stepdown, b-leadership-transfer; f-term-vote, f-leadership-validity). Connection covers the startIndex commitment rule, configuration-driven quorum membership, and prefix-validated support with ErrLeadershipLost answering all pending futures on step-down.\\n- 7 Activities (A1-A7), 16 Behaviors, 6 Facts with consistent derived indexes, and 4 sourced Surfaces (heartbeat fast path, timeoutNow, transport plumbing, deferred bootstrap/recovery).\\n- Three open_details kept as leads, not core gaps: the off-thread heartbeat fast path vs the documented main-thread-only appendEntries; timeoutNow campaigning without consulting term/sender; appendConfigurationEntry publishing the new latest configuration after a StoreLogs failure already set state Follower.\\n- First Candidate (action=continue, needs_specific_evidence, source_review): whether the transport heartbeat fast path is serialized with the main loop before it updates the receiver's term/state/leader, with counterevidence that pure heartbeats skip the log/commit/configuration branches and that the fields touched are atomic or mutex-protected.\\n\\nPreflight `validate` returned valid=true with no diagnostics. This is a validated draft; acceptance, formal execution and evidence remain with the controller.\"\n}"}}
